# API & Integrations

## Server endpoint (the only one)

`POST /api/paystack-verify` → `functions/api/paystack-verify.js`

- Purpose: verify a Paystack transaction server-side after the client-side popup
  completes, so success can't be spoofed from the browser.
- Reads `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` from `env` (set in Cloudflare dashboard).
- Full contract in `docs/api.md`.

## Client-side third-party calls (no server involved)

- **Paystack popup checkout** — `src/components/forms/PartnershipEngine.tsx`. Card
  entry happens inside Paystack's own iframe (keeps the site PCI-scope-clean). Public
  key + subaccount code are in client code (safe to expose). Verification is the
  server function above.
- **Debbie AI (Start Here)** — calls **Groq** directly from the client using a public
  key. No server proxy.
- **Contact** — uses `mailto:`; there is no form-submission backend.
- **Events CTA** — links out to an external events site; not served here.

## Rule

Don't add a Next.js API route or middleware — the static export can't run them. Any new
server behavior is a Cloudflare Pages Function under `functions/api/*`. See
[backend](backend.mdc).
